{"data":{"body":"**[P2] Validate duration types before applying the regex**\n\nThe matcher applies this regex to `str(actual)`, so `durationMs: \"1000\"` passes just like the number `1000`. The three operation duration assertions have the same gap, allowing an exporter that serializes measurements as strings to pass conformance. Validate the JSON numeric type and non-negative duration constraint explicitly, excluding booleans, and add digit-only string rejection tests for all four duration fields.","comment_node_id":"PRRC_kwDOTa1Cx88AAAABA5i2Yw","finding_digest":"8c91063332809ae5f228e1eaa6b3c4fce4ea27dd051b356a7ad5af70fac47040","finding_id":"arf_v1_rsiqmmzsqcnol4ri4hvknm6e7t","finding_key":"telemetry/telemetry-1.yaml::telemetryassertions::incomplete-record-schema","identity_key":"telemetry/telemetry-1.yaml::telemetryassertions::incomplete-record-schema","line":43,"observation_digest":"19f097b3d5d545bb69be84fff4f4b2a221a225067d02b44abc1f5622f7bd0148","observation_id":"aro_v1_dhyjpm6v2vc3w2n6qt77j5fsui","path":"packages/aws-durable-execution-conformance-tests-telemetry/test-requirements/telemetry/telemetry-1.yaml","prior_finding_id":"arf_v1_rsiqmmzsqcnol4ri4hvknm6e7t","published_at":"2026-10-23T01:43:29Z","review_id":"arr_v1_tpqsly2b6kbbk2u7bwq5ddpcvo","reviewed_base_sha":"eae1a45ee3c1fdfea4e2567071c5f7455e1e1b05","reviewed_head_sha":"fd3a2f8c2d4cac69c9970193b7fa00cd6cc4e721","reviewer":"codex","start_line":43,"suggestion_id":""},"pull_request":{"number":144},"record_id":"art_v1_2xmtdpec4evptcotfgk6saiyqj","record_type":"finding_observed","recorded_at":"2026-10-23T01:43:29Z","repository":{"full_name":"aws/aws-durable-execution-conformance-tests","id":1303200455},"schema_version":1}
